 "segments": [
  "[  0.00-  4.36] He slammed the brakes on the highway, and the car behind him smashes right into his bumper.",
  "[  4.64-  8.88] He climbs out, holding his neck and limping, because he figures whoever hits you from behind",
  "[  8.88- 12.62] always gets the blame, and sure enough, their insurance pays for his car,",
  "[ 12.82- 15.76] his doctor, and a nice fat check for all that pain he's in.",
  "[ 15.88- 18.50] So, the next week, he does it again with a different car.",
  "[ 18.66- 22.06] He picks them carefully, a guy on his phone, a kid who just got his license,",
  "[ 22.34- 23.90] anyone driving a little too close.",
  "[ 24.16- 27.60] Then, he brings a buddy, who drives right beside you so you can't swerve.",
  "[ 27.60- 31.74] The money comes in so fast, he buys a nicer car, just to crash that one too.",
  "[ 31.92- 34.10] Eventually, the insurance company starts calling.",
  "[ 34.38- 36.72] Sir, this is your fifth neck injury this year.",
  "[ 36.88- 40.80] Yeah, I've got a really weak neck, but it's his word against the guy who hit him,",
  "[ 40.88- 43.32] and he's counting on everyone blaming the guy in the back.",
  "[ 43.50- 46.68] Then, one rainy morning, he picks a quiet guy in an old car,",
  "[ 46.90- 49.76] slams on his brakes, and out he comes, clutching his neck.",
  "[ 49.90- 52.50] But the quiet guy doesn't yell, and he doesn't even get out.",
  "[ 52.64- 54.96] He just points at a little box taped to his windshield.",
  "[ 54.96- 59.74] It's a camera, and it filmed an empty road and a man breaking for absolutely nothing.",
  "[ 60.02- 61.90] And that's how the dash cam was invented."
